# this container's mounts + service, both lanes
#
# build-spec — per-port runtime declaration, sourced by the shared resolver.
# (Name `build-spec` is a PLACEHOLDER pending a rename.) Baked at
# /opt/resources/build-spec; the repo holds one per target (targets/<port>/build-spec).
#
# This is SOURCED bash — plain arrays/vars, zero dependencies. The shared entrypoint
# (droste-entrypoint.sh) sources droste-resolve.sh, sources this file, then runs
# resolve::apply_spec in this EXACT order:
#
#   ensure /opt/config (warn if unbound) + /opt/program (auto-vol + warn)
#          + /opt/program-cache (warn if unbound)
#     -> SURFACES + OVERLAYS + CACHES   (mounted; server lane only, no-op in distrobox)
#     -> CRITICAL                       (hard-error if unbound + ALLOW_EPHEMERAL escape)
#     -> OPTIONAL                       (INFO once + create marker file)
#     -> templates.yaml seeding         (AFTER mounts)
#     -> CFG_FILE source                (if declared and the file exists)
#     -> PRE_LAUNCH function            (if declared)
#   [apply_spec ends here; the two doors then do the same two things]
#     -> download watcher               (dlwatch::launch — AFTER apply_spec because
#                                        its off switch lives in CFG_FILE)
#     -> exec SERVICE                   (or the user's `run IMAGE <cmd>`, which wins)
#
# The distrobox-lane init hook runs the SAME order and then hands SERVICE to
# droste-serve.sh, which starts it in the background only when the box's own
# <box>.cfg says DROSTE_<APP>_STARTUP_ENABLED is on (merged one-container shape;
# see base/resolve/droste-serve.sh).
#
# NOTE the two reads of that ONE file, and do not conflate them — it is the defect
# class the naming exists to prevent. `droste::cfg_apply` (the CFG_FILE step above)
# APPLIES the app settings through a child shell; `droste::cfg_get` PARSES a single
# serve setting and never sources. The serve settings are read the second way, so
# the wiring must never reach for $DROSTE_<APP>_PORT and friends in the environment.
# (The retired server.env, and its single SERVE=1 knob, are both gone.)
#
# All content SEEDING (default files/dirs) is owned by templates.yaml, NOT this file.
# There is deliberately no DEFAULTS row. Every path below is EXPLICIT and ABSOLUTE.
#
# ── WHICH ROOT A ROW USES IS ITS CLASS DECLARATION ───────────────────────────
# Four container-side roots; the prefix of a src/upper is the whole classification,
# so nothing downstream has to guess from a path's contents (see droste-resolve.sh).
# THE QUESTION THAT PICKS ONE IS "WHAT GETS IT BACK?" (Jei, s79):
#   /opt/config         THE CONFIG SURFACE, per box — NOTHING gets it back. <box>.cfg
#                       and its .example, vllm_config.yaml, jupyter_server_config.py,
#                       comfyui's extra_model_paths.yaml. The most hand-authored
#                       artifacts in the project. Never wiped, never overwritten.
#                       ⚠️ NO ROW TYPE BELOW PLACES ANYTHING HERE. The INSTALLER
#                       writes these files, from this port's templates.yaml
#                       `if_missing` section; a spec only NAMES one, via CFG_FILE.
#   /opt/program        PROGRAM DATA, per box — a REINSTALL or a RE-RUN gets it back,
#                       at a cost. The venv upper (and its .work sibling), comfyui's
#                       custom_nodes upper + model-tree + datasets, ds4 internal/ +
#                       cockpit/, logs/. NOTHING WE SHIP EVER EMPTIES THIS ROOT OR
#                       OFFERS TO (ruled, s79).
#   /opt/program-cache  PROGRAM CACHE, per box — FREE regen, the program rebuilds it
#                       unasked: copy-mode materializations, tmp, llama slots, ds4
#                       kv-disk, the state/ server dir, the compute-cache fallback
#                       under compute/. The installer may empty this ROOT WHOLE with
#                       the user's consent — so never put anything here that a user
#                       would miss.
#   /opt/caches         SHARED compute caches across boxes; never written to by a
#                       spec directly, only reached by the CACHES rewrite below.
# A .work dir is ALWAYS a sibling of its own upper (kernel: workdir and upperdir must
# share a filesystem), so it follows that upper's root — not the class table.
# ⚠️ THE VENV UPPER WAS ON /opt/program-cache UNTIL s79, i.e. on the one root the
# installer wipes, and that cost a working box. Do not move it back.

# ── SERVICE (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The service argv. Bash array; exec'd verbatim unless the user passes a command.
#
# TIMING: this file is plain sourced bash, so the array's words expand at
# SPEC-SOURCE time — BEFORE CFG_FILE is sourced. A SERVICE that must carry
# env-file-derived pieces (e.g. $DROSTE_LLAMA_EXTRA_ARGS) cannot reference them here;
# use the SERVICE-REBUILD pattern instead: declare a placeholder argv, then have
# PRE_LAUNCH (which runs AFTER CFG_FILE) rebuild it — see PRE_LAUNCH below.
SERVICE=( python /opt/ComfyUI/main.py --listen 0.0.0.0 --port 8188 )

# ── HEALTH_PATH / HEALTH_ACCEPT / HEALTH_START (optional) ────────────────────
# The container-side probe endpoint used by droste-healthcheck.sh (podman
# healthcheck in the merged one-container shape). The probe builds its URL from
# three things, none of them this file: the ADDRESS from serve::probe_addr (which
# follows DROSTE_<APP>_HOST, so a narrowed box is probed where it actually listens),
# the SCHEME by detection (serve::probe retries the other one and caches the answer
# per container start, so TLS needs no declaration), and the PORT from the box's
# <box>.cfg via droste::cfg_get, defaulting to this spec's SERVE_PORT_DEFAULT.
#   HEALTH_PATH   request path. Default "/".
#   HEALTH_ACCEPT "ok"  (default) = healthy on 2xx/3xx;
#                 "any"           = healthy on ANY HTTP response, for servers whose
#                                   only unauthenticated answer is a redirect or a
#                                   403 (jupyter). Connection refused/timeout is
#                                   ALWAYS unhealthy.
#   HEALTH_START  this box's --health-start-period, as a Go duration ("45m"). NOT a
#                 probe endpoint: it is the box's copy of the grace the INSTALLER
#                 gives podman at create time (installer/contract.sh's
#                 BOX_HEALTH_START), and it exists here because the probe runs inside
#                 the box and cannot read the host's installer. Its one reader is
#                 serve::restart_window_bound, which bounds the grace window a
#                 `server_restart` gets before podman's --health-on-failure=restart
#                 would bounce the whole container (B17). Absent = the library's own
#                 fallback, DROSTE_SERVE_RESTART_WINDOW_FALLBACK.
#                 🚨 IT IS A SECOND COPY OF A NUMBER AND MUST MATCH THE FIRST —
#                 g1lab/probebudget.sh reads both ends and reddens, naming the box.
# Pick a route that means "ready to serve", not merely "process alive": with
# --health-on-failure=restart, a wrong path (a 404 route) restart-loops the box.
HEALTH_PATH="/"
HEALTH_ACCEPT="ok"
HEALTH_START=""

# ── CFG_FILE (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute path to a file sourced right before PRE_LAUNCH. Used by llama/ds4 whose
# config is an env file — written onto /opt/config on the HOST by the installer, from
# the `if_missing` entries of this port's templates.yaml, before the box has ever run.
# ⚠️ ITS BASENAME IS THE BOX'S NAME, BY CONTRACT: the file is named for the BOX
# (`<box>.cfg`) while the settings inside it are named for the APPLICATION. That is
# what droste::box_name derives the two log names from, so a spec whose CFG_FILE is
# not `<box>.cfg` silently renames this box's logs.
# The image does not create it; serve::read_config reports an absent one.
# The resolver sources it under `set -a`, so plain VAR= lines are EXPORTED and
# survive the exec into the service (ports may still belt-and-braces re-export in
# PRE_LAUNCH so the spec stays self-sufficient under other callers).
# Leave "" if unused.
CFG_FILE=""
# CFG_FILE="/opt/config/llama.cfg"

# ── OVERLAYS (optional) — <upper>:<lower> ────────────────────────────────────
# Kernel overlayfs mounted OVER the baked <lower> dir; user writes land in <upper>
# (a host-volume subpath, persisted). Server lane only. Use where the baked lower is
# load-bearing (the whole venv, comfyui custom_nodes). upper = volume side,
# lower = baked app dir. Overlay the WHOLE venv (captures bin/ entry-points too and
# avoids pinning a pythonX.Y path), not just site-packages.
# CLASS: BOTH uppers are PROGRAM — a pip install is re-runnable at a COST, which is
# not the same as free, and the user's own node picks and edits are the same kind of
# thing one step further from free. Neither root is ever emptied by the installer.
OVERLAYS=(
    "/opt/program/venv:/opt/venv"
    "/opt/program/custom_nodes:/opt/ComfyUI/custom_nodes"
)

# ── SURFACES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ───────────────────────────────────────
# Plain bind of a volume subpath (src) onto an app-side path (dest). Server lane
# only. Use for container-specific state with no baked content to preserve (e.g.
# the scanner model-tree). src created if absent.
# CLASS: state surfaces come off /opt/program; a scratch surface (e.g. a tmp dir the
# app fills and never re-reads) comes off /opt/program-cache instead.
# ⚠️ A SURFACE IS THE WRONG SHAPE FOR ANYTHING THE USER MAY WANT TO PLACE THEMSELVES.
# comfyui's user/ was one of these until s79 and is a BIND now, asked about by name
# like input/ and output/ — a surface hides a directory inside another bind, where
# the installer cannot offer it a path of its own.
SURFACES=(
    "/opt/program/model-tree:/opt/ComfyUI/models"
)

# ── CACHES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Same mechanics as SURFACES, kept as a SEPARATE row by design: this is the ONE row
# type whose src can be REWRITTEN. Binds /opt/program-cache/compute/<x> onto a tool's
# default ~/.cache/* path so compute/kernel caches persist with zero env vars.
# Server lane only; silent.
# THE compute/ SUBDIR IS LOAD-BEARING: srcs under it — and only those — are rewritten
# to /opt/caches/<x> when the shared compute-cache volume is bound, so all boxes share
# one kernel-cache store. Program caches that must stay PRIVATE to the box (llama
# slots, ds4 kv-disk) live elsewhere on /opt/program-cache and are declared as
# SURFACES: cache class, but sharing another box's session state is meaningless.
# Home-relative dests use $HOME (NOT a hardcoded /root): the spec is sourced in
# BOTH lanes, and only $HOME resolves correctly in each (server /root, distrobox
# the user's host home).
CACHES=(
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen:$HOME/.cache/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/triton:$HOME/.triton/cache"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/torch:$HOME/.cache/torch"
)

# ── CRITICAL (optional) — <label>:<path> ─────────────────────────────────────
# Hard-error (refuse to start) if <path> is not bound; the message names <label> and
# shows an example bind flag. ALLOW_EPHEMERAL (bare env name, any value) downgrades
# every CRITICAL to a warning and continues ephemeral. Both lanes.
# HF cache is CRITICAL on every port that uses it (unbound => silent 20GB+ re-download).
# Use $HOME for home-relative paths (lane-correct — under distrobox's whole-$HOME
# bind the ancestor-walk correctly reads them as bound; /root never would be).
CRITICAL=(
    "input:/opt/ComfyUI/input"
    "output:/opt/ComfyUI/output"
    "hf-cache:$HOME/.cache/huggingface"
)

# ── OPTIONAL (optional) — <label>:<path>[:<marker>] ──────────────────────────
# Tell-once-don't-nag. If <path> is unpopulated (empty or marker-only) AND the marker
# is absent: emit an INFO line and CREATE the marker (body = templates dir file named
# like the marker basename, else a built-in one-liner). Unpopulated + marker present:
# silent. Populated: silent. Marker defaults to <path>/.droste-informed if omitted.
OPTIONAL=(
    "opt-models:/opt/models:/opt/models/mount_shared_models_here"
)

# ── DOWNLOAD_WATCH (optional) — extra directories to watch for downloads ─────
# EXTRA roots for the download announcer (droste-dlwatch.sh, N24). Not a mount and
# not a bind: purely a list of directories the watcher globs for partial files
# (*.incomplete, *.downloadInProgress) so a transfer in one of them is announced in
# `podman logs <box>`.
#
# TWO ROOTS ARE ALWAYS WATCHED AND NEED NO ROW: $HOME/.cache/huggingface (the hub
# cache, a CRITICAL row on every port) and $HOME/.cache/llama.cpp (llama's second
# cache for -mu/-dr, which has no row of its own by design — R10: watch it, do not
# declare it). This row is for the ones only the port knows about, and today that
# means a hub `--local-dir` target: ds4's DS4_GGUF_DIR fetches land in
# <dir>/.cache/huggingface/download/ and are invisible to the two defaults.
#
# ⚠️ TIMING, AND IT IS THE SAME TRAP AS SERVICE'S. This file is sourced BEFORE
# CFG_FILE, so a value that depends on a user setting cannot be written here — set
# it in PRE_LAUNCH instead, which runs after. The doors read this array AFTER
# apply_spec returns, so a PRE_LAUNCH assignment is seen.
# ⚠️ A ROOT THAT DOES NOT EXIST IS SILENT, not an error: it costs one failed glob
# per tick. Declaring a path a user may never create is therefore free.
DOWNLOAD_WATCH=()
# DOWNLOAD_WATCH=( "$HOME/ds4-gguf" )

# ── PRE_LAUNCH (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Name of a bash FUNCTION defined in THIS file; run after CFG_FILE, before exec.
# Examples: comfyui model_scanner sync; ds4 DROSTE_DS4_* -> argv translation.
PRE_LAUNCH=""
# PRE_LAUNCH="port_pre_launch"
# port_pre_launch() {
#     model_scanner sync
# }
#
# THE SERVICE-REBUILD PATTERN (how llama/ds4 pass env-derived args):
# SERVICE expands at spec-source time, BEFORE CFG_FILE — so a spec whose argv
# depends on env-file values declares a bare placeholder up top and rebuilds the
# array in PRE_LAUNCH, which runs AFTER the env file is sourced:
#
#   SERVICE=( llama-server )                       # placeholder argv
#   CFG_FILE="/opt/config/llama.cfg"
#   PRE_LAUNCH="port_pre_launch"
#   port_pre_launch() {
#       # belt-and-braces: re-export the vars the binary reads from its
#       # environment (the resolver's set -a source already exports CFG_FILE
#       # assignments; this also covers vars set outside the env file).
#       local v
#       for v in $(compgen -v LLAMA_ || true); do export "${v?}"; done
#       # rebuild the argv now that env-file values are known
#       # shellcheck disable=SC2206
#       SERVICE=( llama-server ${DROSTE_LLAMA_EXTRA_ARGS:-} )
#   }
#
# The entrypoint execs whatever SERVICE holds AFTER PRE_LAUNCH returns.
